From e2132d71a10d09c8f19baad8059740c68742cc6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@local>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:22:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/38] kebab: XNU-001a-2 RAM FAT test volume (read-only
 BlockIo producer)

Adds XnuRamDiskDxe: reads the embedded FAT12 image from the firmware
volume by GUID (GetSectionFromAnyFv) and exposes it as a read-only
EFI_BLOCK_IO_PROTOCOL device so the existing DiskIo/Partition/Fat stack
can present it as SimpleFileSystem.

Design notes:
- Self-contained: no HII, no ASL. (EDK2 RamDiskDxe was evaluated first but
  cannot be built here: it needs iasl for RamDisk.asl and FileExplorerLib,
  neither available in this environment.)
- WriteBlocks returns EFI_WRITE_PROTECTED; the backing buffer is never
  modified and stays allocated for the RAM disk lifetime.
- Depex TRUE, placed in [FV.FvMain] (not APRIORI).
- ReadyToBoot only *observes*: scoped ConnectController on our own handle,
  then OpenVolume/Open/Read of XNU-TEST.TXT and content comparison.

Test volume: 512 KiB FAT12, file XNU-TEST.TXT (112 bytes),
image sha256 f53571afc7712bf93b811d50260958308c7844beb25dd40e0031139151614b62.
